texts.NASB95:
Woe to you, O destroyer,
While you were not destroyed;
And he who is treacherous, while others did not deal treacherously with him.
As soon as you finish destroying, you will be destroyed;
As soon as you cease to deal treacherously, others will deal treacherously with you.

texts.NKJV:
Woe to you who plunder, though you have not been plundered;
And you who deal treacherously, though they have not dealt treacherously with you!
When you cease plundering,
You will be plundered;
When you make an end of dealing treacherously,
They will deal treacherously with you.

texts.NASB95:
And He will be the stability of your times,
A wealth of salvation, wisdom and knowledge;
The fear of the Lord is his treasure.

texts.NKJV:
Wisdom and knowledge will be the stability of your times,
And the strength of salvation;
The fear of the Lord is His treasure.

texts.ESV:
and he will be the stability of your times,
    abundance of salvation, wisdom, and knowledge;
    the fear of the Lord is Zion's treasure.

The highways lie waste;
    the traveler ceases.
Covenants are broken;
    cities are despised;
    there is no regard for man.

The land mourns and languishes;
    Lebanon is confounded and withers away;
Sharon is like a desert,
    and Bashan and Carmel shake off their leaves.

texts.NASB95:
Look down from heaven and see from Your holy and glorious habitation;
Where are Your zeal and Your mighty deeds?
The stirrings of Your heart and Your compassion are restrained toward me.

texts.ESV:
There is no one who calls upon your name,
    who rouses himself to take hold of you;
for you have hidden your face from us,
    and have made us melt in the hand of our iniquities.

texts.NASB95:
But now, O Lord, You are our Father,
We are the clay, and You our potter;
And all of us are the work of Your hand.

texts.NKJV:
But now, O Lord,
You are our Father;
We are the clay, and You our potter;
And all we are the work of Your hand.

texts.ESV:
But now, O Lord, you are our Father;
    we are the clay, and you are our potter;
    we are all the work of your hand.

texts.NASB95:
Do not be angry beyond measure, O Lord,
Nor remember iniquity forever;
Behold, look now, all of us are Your people.

texts.NKJV:
Do not be furious, O Lord,
Nor remember iniquity forever;
Indeed, please look—we all are Your people!

texts.ESV:
Your holy cities have become a wilderness;
    Zion has become a wilderness,
    Jerusalem a desolation.

texts.NKJV:
The waters surrounded me, even to my soul;
The deep closed around me;
Weeds were wrapped around my head.

texts.ESV:
The waters closed in over me to take my life;
    the deep surrounded me;
weeds were wrapped about my head

texts.NKJV:
I went down to the moorings of the mountains;
The earth with its bars closed behind me forever;
Yet You have brought up my life from the pit,
O Lord, my God.

O Lord, I have heard Your speech and was afraid;
O Lord, revive Your work in the midst of the years!
In the midst of the years make it known;
In wrath remember mercy.

texts.ESV:
O Lord, I have heard the report of you,
    and your work, O Lord, do I fear.
In the midst of the years revive it;
    in the midst of the years make it known;
    in wrath remember mercy.

texts.NASB95:
His radiance is like the sunlight;
He has rays flashing from His hand,
And there is the hiding of His power.

texts.NKJV:
His brightness was like the light;
He had rays flashing from His hand,
And there His power was hidden.

texts.ESV:
His brightness was like the light;
    rays flashed from his hand;
    and there he veiled his power.

He stood and measured the earth;
    he looked and shook the nations;
then the eternal mountains were scattered;
    the everlasting hills sank low.
    His were the everlasting ways.

texts.NKJV:
Your bow was made quite ready;
Oaths were sworn over Your arrows. Selah 
You divided the earth with rivers.

texts.ESV:
The mountains saw you and writhed;
    the raging waters swept on;
the deep gave forth its voice;
    it lifted its hands on high.

texts.NASB95:
Sun and moon stood in their places;
They went away at the light of Your arrows,
At the radiance of Your gleaming spear.

texts.NKJV:
The sun and moon stood still in their habitation;
At the light of Your arrows they went,
At the shining of Your glittering spear.

When I heard, my body trembled;
My lips quivered at the voice;
Rottenness entered my bones;
And I trembled in myself,
That I might rest in the day of trouble.
When he comes up to the people,
He will invade them with his troops.

texts.ESV:
I hear, and my body trembles;
    my lips quiver at the sound;
rottenness enters into my bones;
    my legs tremble beneath me.
Yet I will quietly wait for the day of trouble
    to come upon people who invade us.
